// Cross-disease neurodegeneration network — curated relationship graph.
//
// Each node represents a gene/protein from the neurodigineration panel. `prevalence`
// (0–1) drives the visual box size — it encodes how prominent the gene is
// in its primary disease, accounting for both monogenic cause-prevalence
// and risk-modifier strength. The intent is: the boxes you see biggest
// are the names a clinician thinks of first when the disease is mentioned.
//
// Each edge represents a real biological relationship between two genes:
// either a direct molecular interaction (kinase/substrate, receptor/ligand,
// complex partners) or a shared-mechanism / shared-disease co-implication.
// The `kind` field colours the edge so the viewer can read "this is a
// substrate relationship" vs "this is a cross-disease coincidence."
//
// Coverage as of Round 7: 324 nodes and 510 edges across 11 disease groups
// (PD, AD, ALS/FTD, HD/polyQ, Prion, Lysosomal storage, NBIA, Tauopathy
// PSP/CBD/FTLD-tau, HSP, CMT, and a Shared core for the cross-cutting
// machinery — autophagy, mitophagy, secretases, microglial axis, complement,
// SNARE/SV, stress granules, ER-mitochondria contacts, lipid metabolism,
// the UPR/integrated stress response, dopamine handling, NCL/MPS lysosomal
// enzymes, axon-death (SARM1/NMNAT2), and CSF/fluid biomarkers).
// Round 6 synced the 17 genes that were trainable in the model panel but
// missing from the graph, then added ~90 new proteins to both the graph and
// the panel — so the network node set and the trainable panel are now 1:1.
// Of the 474 edges, ~167 are marked `tentative: true` (rendered dotted) —
// flagged as candidates for SME validation rather than load-bearing claims.
// Every Round-6 edge carries pmids: [] (citations pending validation via the
// rate-the-edge loop).
//
// Round 7 (data hygiene + orphan rescue):
// - The graph is now a single connected component. Before, SOD1, EPHA1,
//   CLN6 and CLN8 had no edges at all, and a 14-gene lysosomal-enzyme
//   cluster, the CMT myelin trio and GIGYF2/EIF4G1 floated as islands.
// - Two new directional kinds: 'enzyme-substrate' and 'transcriptional'.
//   Most of the old 'kinase-substrate' edges were proteases, E3 ligases,
//   phosphatases or TFs; those were reclassified and substrate→enzyme
//   arrows flipped. Parkin→alpha-synuclein ubiquitination is now tentative.
// - Three duplicate edges removed; 13 nodes added (Prion, NBIA, HSP, CMT,
//   CCS for SOD1, GFAP as a fluid biomarker) and mirrored in the panel.
// - New edges carry pmids: []. PMIDs we could not verify are left out
//   rather than guessed. The network page's live PubMed panel is the
//   intended way to back-fill them.

